Keeps the items of a list that a test accepts. The input is the pair [pred xs]: pred is a function of one argument that gives nonzero for an item to keep, and the output is the kept items, in order.
---

---
(fn p
  (letrec f (fn l
        (if (? l) ~
            (if ((head p) (head l))
                [(head l) (f (tail l))]
                (f (tail l)))))
    (f (tail p))))
---
[(fn x (< x 3)) 1 5 2 4 ~] => [1 2 ~] fuel 100000
[(fn x (< x 3)) ~] => ~ fuel 100000
[(fn x 0) 1 2 ~] => ~ fuel 100000
